/**
 * Plan your first analysis: the shared content and decision logic.
 *
 * One source of truth for four surfaces, so they cannot drift:
 *   1. /start, the public scoping flow and the checklist it prints.
 *   2. The economist-led onboarding call outline.
 *   3. The tailored one-page checklist (the print view of a result).
 *   4. The internal coordinator brief, generated by
 *      `npm run docs:plan` into docs/onboarding/.
 *
 * Three rules hold everywhere in this file.
 *
 * ORGANIZATIONAL COMPLEXITY AND DATA READINESS ARE SEPARATE.
 * They are scored independently and shown as two readings. A complex
 * organization often has excellent records; a single-location operation
 * often cannot reach its own. Collapsing them into one score would put
 * organizations into an onboarding path neither dimension justifies.
 *
 * NOTHING HERE PROMISES AN OUTPUT THE MODEL DOES NOT PRODUCE.
 * Every capability carries a `status`. `available` means the product
 * accepts the input and reports the result today. `proposed` means the
 * behavior is specified and not yet wired through the product. `research`
 * means the treatment is still open. Claims marked `review` are awaiting
 * economist sign-off and must not be reworded into product promises
 * before that happens. What the product does today, verified in
 * teim-app and teim-engine while this file was written:
 *   - One analysis covers one region and one reporting year. More
 *     geographies or more years run as a series of analyses.
 *     (src/features/intake/geographyMulti.js, multiYear.js)
 *   - The run anchors to one state, with an optional homelands subset
 *     and a county list resolved from the addresses of the operations.
 *     (server/contracts/runRequest.js, server/engine/teimEngineProtocol.js)
 *   - One primary sector is carried per operation, so operations that
 *     should be reported in their own sectors are recorded separately.
 *     (src/features/intake/submissionAdapter.js, getPrimaryCategory)
 *   - Local purchasing is estimated from regional trade data. Vendor
 *     level spending and a manual local purchase percentage are not
 *     inputs the model accepts. (teim-engine input_framework.md 6.1)
 *
 * NO INVENTED CONFIDENCE. Coverage indicators are counts and shares with
 * a named denominator. Where the denominator is unknown, the indicator is
 * not shown. No percentage improvements, no error bars, no confidence
 * scores.
 */

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
 * 1. The scoping questions
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

